{
  "message": "The good news is that the check found no failures, and the access boundaries we drew all hold together, including the read-only CRM and the escalation path. It's blocked because 8 components don't have a generated implementation yet: the web app, sign-in, API, orchestrator and catalog still need code, and the existing browser, ticket queue and CRM each need a plan for how we reference or connect to them. I won't hide any of that or call the setup validated. A supported setup only exists if we choose keyword search, and even then the ticket and CRM connections and the escalation would stay as product engineering work.\n\nShould the assistant find answers by matching keywords across a small set of approved articles (up to about 100), or by searching for meaning across a larger library?",
